Make codesigning and archive processing work under strict remote
execution.

Default codesign_inputs to //apple:sdk_tool_files so that codesigning
actions (ProcessAndSign, SignBinary, and bundletool-embedded signing)
declare the cross-toolchain's xcrun/codesign/zip binaries as inputs.
Local no-sandbox execution resolves them from the execroot either way,
but strict remote execution only stages declared inputs.

Also resolve relative PATH entries in the process-and-sign script before
it changes directories: the toolchain bin directory is provided as an
execroot-relative PATH entry, which stops resolving once the script
pushd's into the archive root to zip the bundle.

Also expose sdk_tool_files on AppleMacToolsToolchainInfo and feed them to
the SwiftStdlibCopy action, replacing its no-remote/no-sandbox opt-out:
with the tools declared as inputs the action can run remotely, which a
macOS host requires because the staged tool binaries are Linux
executables.

diff --git a/apple/internal/rule_attrs.bzl b/apple/internal/rule_attrs.bzl
--- a/apple/internal/rule_attrs.bzl
+++ b/apple/internal/rule_attrs.bzl
@@ -188,6 +188,7 @@
         _common_linking_api_attrs(deps_cfg = deps_cfg),
         {
             "codesign_inputs": attr.label_list(
+                default = [Label("//apple:sdk_tool_files")],
                 doc = """
 A list of dependencies targets that provide inputs that will be used by
 `codesign` (referenced with `codesignopts`).
diff --git a/tools/bundletool/process_and_sign.sh.template b/tools/bundletool/process_and_sign.sh.template
--- a/tools/bundletool/process_and_sign.sh.template
+++ b/tools/bundletool/process_and_sign.sh.template
@@ -6,6 +6,17 @@
 # 2. This script is passed arguments but they are *NOT* used, the arguments
 #    are there to allow action logging to have some visibility into what the
 #    actions running the script is doing each time.
+
+# Resolve relative PATH entries (execroot-relative toolchain directories)
+# against the initial working directory so that tools stay reachable after
+# the script changes directories to archive the bundle.
+_abs_path=""
+IFS=':' read -r -a _path_entries <<< "$PATH"
+for _entry in "${_path_entries[@]}"; do
+  [[ "$_entry" == /* ]] || _entry="$PWD/$_entry"
+  _abs_path="${_abs_path:+$_abs_path:}$_entry"
+done
+export PATH="$_abs_path"
 
 # The path where the archive should be created, including the name of the
 # archive itself.
